Z||000005||stimpy||05-14-2001||04:44 PM||||If your car is running right, then a new chip or headers is not going to be the magic bullet. I'm tending to think there are other issues. You know, I've never got to hear your car run. I think we may need to do an intervention...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||05-14-2001||05:03 PM||||I agree - something is way wrong - 3.4L you should be running what, about 200HP?<P>and you got shut down by a 2000 lb car with a 55 HP engine?<P>maybe something really simple is wrong. did you ever check your gas pedal to make sure that when the pedal is on the floor that the butterfly is WFO?<P>clutch slipping?<P>a couple of cylinders not firing?<P>exhaust completely blocked off?<P>  you are either pulling our collective leg here or something is hosed on your car. I have owned stock aircooled VW beetles and I can tell you, even with the crappy way my 85 SE V6 2.8L auto is running right now, it will blow a stock VW bug off the road (they have a top speed of 88mph you know, seriously!)||||reg||1
